COMMENT ON TABLE public.amazon_ads_campaign_daily IS 'Amazon Ads (Sponsored Products, Brands, Brand video, Display) by day, campaign and ad group, de-duplicated v3 > v2 > v1 per campaign-day; the daily spend sum equals proj_feed_amazon.ad_spend. Grain: one row per (day, marketplace, campaign_id, ad_group_id, ad_type); ad_group_id is '''' for types that report no ad group. Source: etl.feeds amazon_ads_campaign_daily (ExpandFi warehouse, merchant 1452: amazon_ads_campaign_data). Refresh: feeds service 21:00 UTC (python -m etl.feeds run), trailing 21 days; each run replaces its window, an empty pull writes nothing. Coverage: 2025-12-30 (Sponsored Products v3) to yesterday; Sponsored Display from 2026-01-29, Sponsored Brands from 2026-02-03. Rows with no spend, impressions, clicks or sales are not stored.. Caveats: ad_type comes from the report type. Rows from the older v1 report that ExpandFi files under spCampaigns also hold Sponsored Brands, Sponsored Display and Full-Funnel campaigns, so they read ''sp''. | Amazon has no ad-attributed revenue on one basis: sales_reported is Sponsored Products 14-day sales and the single reported sales figure of the other types. Do not add it to Meta or Google revenue. | The 1/7/14/30-day columns exist for Sponsored Products v3 only; older generations store zeros there, so they are NULL here. NULL is not zero. | Campaigns carry no product in the report: product_slug is the ASIN the campaign name contains (about 88% of spend); campaigns such as ''All Products'' and ''Full-Funnel'' have NULL.';
