COMMENT ON TABLE public.amazon_orders_asin_daily IS 'Actual Amazon.com orders by day, ASIN and channel (Amazon.com and Amazon.com B2B): units, orders, revenue and new customers, on the same basis as proj_feed_amazon. Grain: one row per (day, asin, sales_channel). Source: etl.feeds amazon_orders_asin_daily (ExpandFi warehouse, merchant 1452: sales joined to customers). Refresh: feeds service 21:00 UTC (python -m etl.feeds run), trailing 21 days; each run replaces its window, an empty pull writes nothing. Coverage: 2024-09-24 to about 2 days ago (late orders post for about two weeks). Caveats: Purchase-date basis. New customer = the order is on the customer''s first purchase day (customers.cohort_day), the rule of proj_feed_amazon; orders without a customer row are excluded, as there. | Daily units and revenue sums equal proj_feed_amazon. orders counts distinct orders per ASIN, so an order with two ASINs counts under both: do not sum orders across ASINs. | Revenue is total_amount_usd (tax and shipping as Amazon reports the line), before refunds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.day IS 'Purchase day (Pacific, as ExpandFi stores it).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.asin IS 'ASIN of the order line ('''' when the line has none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.sales_channel IS 'Amazon.com | Amazon.com B2B.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.product_slug IS 'vita-bull | beef-liver | boneflex | vita-belle | vital-flow; NULL when the ASIN (or the campaign name''s ASIN) is not an Amazon.com ASIN of amazon_asin_products.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.product_name IS 'Display name of product_slug (Vita Bull, Beef Liver, Boneflex, Vita Belle, Vital Flow).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.orders IS 'Distinct orders with this ASIN that day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.units IS 'Units shipped.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.revenue IS 'Order line revenue, US dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.nc_orders IS 'Orders placed by a customer on their first purchase day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.nc_revenue IS 'Revenue of those orders, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_orders_asin_daily.loaded_at IS 'When the row was loaded.';
COMMENT ON TABLE public.amazon_traffic_daily IS 'Amazon.com account traffic by day: sessions, page views and buy box share (Sales and Traffic report), with ordered units and sales as Amazon counts them. Grain: one row per (day, marketplace_id); US only. Source: etl.feeds amazon_traffic_daily (ExpandFi warehouse, merchant 1452: sales_and_traffic_reports, PARENT rows). Refresh: feeds service 21:00 UTC (python -m etl.feeds run), trailing 14 days; each run replaces its window, an empty pull writes nothing. Coverage: 2024-04-07 to yesterday. Caveats: Account level, not by ASIN (each ASIN row of the source repeats the account total). The latest restatement of each day is kept; recent days move for about a week. | Percentages are 0-100. Ordered units and sales are Amazon''s ordered-product figures, not the shipped orders of amazon_orders_asin_daily.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.amazon_traffic_daily.day IS 'Report day.';
