COMMENT ON VIEW analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly IS 'Read the SUM-vs-MAX rule first. Amazon Brand Analytics Search Query Performance by week: for each search query and each of our ASINs, the query''s market size and our share of impressions, clicks, cart adds and purchases (the organic search signal). Grain: one row per (period_start = Sunday, marketplace_id, asin, query_key). Source: public.amazon_sqp_weekly (ExpandFi merchant 1452). Refresh: feeds service 21:00 UTC (python -m etl.feeds run), trailing 6 weeks; each run replaces its window, an empty pull writes nothing; a week lands about 5 days after its Saturday. Coverage: weeks from 2025-07-13 to the last landed week; 8 ASINs, mostly US. Caveats: SUM vs MAX: total_* columns and search_query_volume are market totals repeated on every ASIN row of a query, so SUM across ASINs overstates them (5 ASIN rows = 5x): use MAX per query and period; to total OUR side SUM the asin_* columns. | Top-100 cap: Amazon reports only about the top 100 queries per ASIN and period. A query that is absent is not in that list, not zero, and a query dropping out looks like a share collapse. | Shares are percent 0-100, not fractions (2.95 = 2.95 percent). | Impressions include sponsored placements: our own ads count in asin_impressions and the shares. Purchases are search-origin and same-day and will not tie to orders. | No organic rank position exists anywhere in the data; the click, cart add and purchase shares are the proxy. | Never sum weekly rows into a month or compare a week with a month: periods overlap in meaning and the query lists differ. | Duplicate source rows (restated re-pulls) are collapsed to the latest; the newest week or month can still be partial for a week or two.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.period_start IS 'First day of the period (Sunday for a week, the 1st for a month).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.period_end IS 'Last day of the period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.marketplace_id IS 'Amazon marketplace id (ATVPDKIKX0DER = US, A1AM78C64UM0Y8 = MX).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.marketplace IS 'US | MX | CA | BR from marketplace_id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin IS 'Our ASIN the shares belong to.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.query_key IS 'The search query lower-cased, trimmed, runs of spaces collapsed to one: the join key to other query tables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.search_query IS 'The query text as Amazon reported it.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.product_slug IS 'vita-bull | beef-liver | boneflex | vita-belle | vital-flow; NULL when the ASIN (or the campaign name''s ASIN) is not an Amazon.com ASIN of amazon_asin_products.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.product_name IS 'Display name of product_slug (Vita Bull, Beef Liver, Boneflex, Vita Belle, Vital Flow).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.is_branded IS 'True when the query names the brand or a product (Lonvera, Vita / Vital Bull, Vita / Vital Belle, Vital Flow, Bone Flex / Boneflex); one rule in etl/feeds/amazon_feeds.py.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.search_query_score IS 'Amazon''s relative popularity score of the query among our ASIN''s queries (1 = most searched).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.search_query_volume IS 'MARKET total: searches for the query on Amazon in the period. Repeated on every ASIN row of the query.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_impressions IS 'MARKET total: impressions of all products for the query (organic and sponsored). Repeated on every ASIN row: never SUM across ASINs, use MAX.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_impressions IS 'Impressions of our ASIN for the query (organic and sponsored).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_impression_share IS 'Our ASIN''s share of the query''s impressions, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_clicks IS 'MARKET total clicks for the query (repeated per ASIN row: MAX).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_click_rate IS 'Market clicks per search, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_clicks IS 'Clicks on our ASIN.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_click_share IS 'Our ASIN''s share of the query''s clicks, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_median_click_price IS 'Market median price of clicked products, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_median_click_price IS 'Median price of our ASIN''s clicks, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_cart_adds IS 'MARKET total cart adds for the query (repeated per ASIN row: MAX).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_cart_add_rate IS 'Market cart adds per search, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_cart_adds IS 'Cart adds of our ASIN.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_cart_add_share IS 'Our ASIN''s share of the query''s cart adds, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_median_cart_add_price IS 'Market median price of carted products, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_median_cart_add_price IS 'Median price of our ASIN''s cart adds, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_purchases IS 'MARKET total purchases for the query (repeated per ASIN row: MAX).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_purchase_rate IS 'Market purchases per search, percent 0-100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_purchases IS 'Purchases of our ASIN (search-origin, same day).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_purchase_share IS 'Our ASIN''s share of the query''s purchases, percent 0-100: the best outcome proxy for organic rank.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.total_median_purchase_price IS 'Market median purchase price, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.asin_median_purchase_price IS 'Median price of our ASIN''s purchases, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN analytics.amazon_search_queries_weekly.loaded_at IS 'When the row was loaded.';
